## Conclusion

Choosing between in-person and online therapy is not about finding the option that is universally best. It is about finding the option that fits your circumstances and helps you engage meaningfully in the therapeutic process.

For some people, meeting with an **in-person therapist** provides the focus, routine, privacy, and face-to-face connection they prefer. For others, online therapy may offer greater convenience and accessibility.

If you are in Houston and considering counseling, exploring an in-person therapy office can be a practical first step. Riaz Counseling offers in-person services through multiple Houston-area locations, along with online therapy across Texas.

Most importantly, give yourself permission to ask questions, consider your preferences, and look for a therapist with whom you can build a collaborative and respectful therapeutic relationship.

